        "text": "Our [GMAT preparation programs](/gmat-preparation) train candidates to leverage test-maker shortcuts: testing extreme boundary values (-1, -1/2, 0, 1/2, 1), backsolving from answer choice (C), and structural estimation before putting pen to paper."
